Context: 2. Salient Points

- (a)
- they can declare separate Home towns independently;
- (b) they can claim LTC for their respective families, viz., while the husband can claim for his parents/ minor brothers/ sisters, the wife can avail for her parents/ minor brothers/ sisters;
- either of the parents can claim the concession for the children
- (c) in a particular block;
- (d) the husband/wife who avails LTC as a member of the family
- of the spouse, cannot claim independently for SELF.  
- GID (18), Rule 7.
